  <string name="sh1_hwreport_title">About hardware rendering</string>
  <string name="sh1_hwreport_body">The hardware backends render the scene mesh on the GPU using the same dither shader and vertex snap as the software renderer; snow, brightness and presentation stay on the CPU.\n\nAccuracy (vs. software, 320×224):\n• OpenGL ES: 44–50 dB PSNR, ~99% bit-exact\n• Vulkan: 44–50 dB PSNR, ~99% bit-exact\n\nBattery (measured, standardized 60 s sequence):\n• CPU work per frame drops by about a third — rasterization moves to the GPU\n• Battery-neutral at the native 320×224 resolution\n• At higher render resolutions: 40–70% lower render energy\n\nThe software renderer remains the default and the accuracy reference.</string>
